  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSSF West Africa: An analysis of conflict dynamics in West Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSSF West Africa Research is a 2-year project that seeks to deepen understanding of potential drivers of regional instability within Coastal West Africa. Through research and policy engagement, this project aims to inform conflict-sensitive programming and integrated security, development, and diplomatic responses in the region. The following objectives guide this research: Objective 1: To understand conflict dynamics in the region Objective 2: To understand the potential implications of these conflict dynamics for security and development in the region. Objective 3: To engage with and influence key stakeholders operating and programming in this region</narrative>
  </description>
